467 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 329 0 R
/T (     A perfume bottle is consist of a container, tube, pump, and a nozzle. When you spray a perfume, the bulb that you press squeezes out the air that is in the tube inside the container through compression. The release of this air creates lower pressure on the nozzle. On the other hand, the pressure in the perfume reservoir remains constant because it is not directly affected by the airflow. That is why, a pressure difference between the nozzle and perfume reservoir is created. )
/E (     A perfume bottle is consist of a container, tube, pump, and a nozzle. When you spray a perfume, the bulb that you press squeezes out the air that is in the tube inside the container through compression. The release of this air creates lower pressure on the nozzle. On the other hand, the pressure in the perfume reservoir remains constant because it is not directly affected by the airflow. That is why, a pressure difference between the nozzle and perfume reservoir is created. )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
468 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
